---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="Nintendo Nitro graphics formats"
  description="NCGR / NCLR / NCER / NSCR / NANR byte layouts as the game ships them. Always wrapped in RESO — never standalone."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: 'File Formats', href: `${base}/field-guide/file-formats/` },
    { label: 'Nitro graphics' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Every Nitro resource lives inside a <a href={`${base}/field-guide/file-formats/reso/`}>RESO</a>
    TOC entry with the corresponding reversed-ASCII <code>type_tag</code>.
    Magic identifiers on disk are little-endian 4-byte words; the reversed
    form spells the intuitive name (e.g. <code>RGCN</code> on disk →
    <code>NCGR</code> read forward).
  </p>

  <h2>NCGR (RGCN) — tile graphics</h2>
  <p>Type tag <code>rgcn</code>. 4,337 instances.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x00</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>magic = <code>"RGCN"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x04</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>byte_order_mark (0xFEFF)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x06</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>version</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x08</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>file_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x0C</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>header_size (0x10)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x0E</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>section_count</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x10</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>section magic = <code>"RAHC"</code> (CHAR)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x14</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>section_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x18</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>tiles_h or <code>0xFFFF</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x1A</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>tiles_w or <code>0xFFFF</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x1C</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>bpp_code (3 = 4bpp / 16-color, 4 = 8bpp / 256-color)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x20</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>mapping_type (1D / 2D OBJ mapping)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x24</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>linear_flag (0 = 8×8 tiled, 1 = linear NCBR)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x28</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>tile_data_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x2C</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>tile_data_offset (typically <code>0x18</code>, relative to <code>RAHC</code> start + 0x18)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x30</code></td><td>—</td><td><code>u8[]</code></td><td>tile pixels</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Tile order in 4bpp tiled mode: 8×8 tiles stored row-major, 4 bits per pixel
    (two pixels per byte, lo-nibble first). Tile-bank index appears in the
    NSCR/NCER reference (10-bit field).
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>0xFFFF</code> dimensions mean "deferred" — for OBJ sprites the
    canvas comes from a paired NCER; for BG screens it comes from a paired
    NSCR (typically 256×192 = 32×24 tiles).
  </p>

  <h2>NCLR (RLCN) — palette</h2>
  <p>Type tag <code>rlcn</code>. 2,600 instances.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x00</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>magic = <code>"RLCN"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x10</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>section magic = <code>"TTLP"</code> (PLTT)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x14</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>section_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x18</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>bpp_code (3 = 16-color, 4 = 256-color)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x1C</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>unknown</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x20</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>palette_data_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x24</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>palette_data_offset (typically <code>0x10</code>, relative)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x28</code></td><td>—</td><td><code>u16[]</code></td><td>BGR555 colors</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Color word layout (16-bit LE): <code>0BBBBB GGGGG RRRRR</code> — 5 bits per
    channel, top bit ignored on hardware. Slot 0 is conventionally transparent
    in OBJ palettes.
  </p>
  <p>
    When <code>section_count ≥ 2</code>, a <code>"PMCP"</code> section follows
    at <code>0x10 + ttlp_size</code>. It maps each 16-color bank to a VRAM
    bank index — when absent, banks are assumed sequential <code>0..N-1</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>NCER (RECN) — cells / OAM</h2>
  <p>Type tag <code>recn</code>. 1,553 instances.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x00</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>magic = <code>"RECN"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x10</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>section magic = <code>"KBEC"</code> (CEBK)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x14</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>section_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x18</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>cell_count</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x1A</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>cell_attr (0 = 8-B entries, 1 = 16-B entries with bbox)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x1C</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>cell_data_offset (relative to <code>KBEC</code>+8)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x20</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>mapping_type</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>Cell entry (8 or 16 bytes):</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>+0x00</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>obj_count</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x02</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>attrs</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x04</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>obj_offset (relative to OAM block)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x08</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>s16</code></td><td>xmax (only if cell_attr=1)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x0A</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>s16</code></td><td>ymax</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x0C</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>s16</code></td><td>xmin</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x0E</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>s16</code></td><td>ymin</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>OAM entry (6 bytes per OBJ):</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Bits</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td rowspan="6"><code>attr0</code> (u16)</td><td>0..7</td><td>y (signed 8-bit, screen coord)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>8</td><td>rotscale</td></tr>
      <tr><td>9</td><td>double_size / disable</td></tr>
      <tr><td>10..11</td><td>obj_mode (normal/blend/window/bitmap)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>12</td><td>mosaic</td></tr>
      <tr><td>13</td><td>depth (0 = 4bpp, 1 = 8bpp)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>14..15</td><td>shape (square / wide / tall / forbidden)</td></tr>
      <tr><td rowspan="4"><code>attr1</code> (u16)</td><td>0..8</td><td>x (signed 9-bit)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>9..11</td><td>rotscale index / unused</td></tr>
      <tr><td>12..13</td><td>hflip, vflip (when rotscale=0)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>14..15</td><td>size</td></tr>
      <tr><td rowspan="3"><code>attr2</code> (u16)</td><td>0..9</td><td>tile index (10 bits → into NCGR tilebank)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>10..11</td><td>priority</td></tr>
      <tr><td>12..15</td><td>palette_bank (4 bits — selects NCLR 16-color bank)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <code>(shape, size)</code> → <code>(width_px, height_px)</code> lookup
    (square 0..3: 8 16 32 64; wide 0..3: 16 32 32 64; tall 0..3: 8 8 16 32).
    Reference: <code>src/translator/_sprite_decode.OBJ_SIZE_LUT</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Optional extra sections after KBEC: <code>"LBAL"</code> (1,778 instances —
    cell state labels like "TAB1_off", "TAB1_on") and <code>"TXEU"</code>
    (1,778 — user extension metadata).
  </p>

  <h2>NSCR (RCSN) — BG screen / tilemap</h2>
  <p>Type tag <code>rcsn</code>. 1,128 instances.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x00</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>magic = <code>"RCSN"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x10</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>section magic = <code>"NRCS"</code> (SCRN)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x14</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>section_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x18</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>width_px (typically 256)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x1A</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>height_px (typically 192)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x1C</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>bpp_code (often 0 — actual bpp comes from paired NCGR)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x20</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32</code></td><td>screen_data_size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x24</code></td><td>—</td><td><code>u16[]</code></td><td>screen cells, row-major (32×24 = 768 cells for 256×192)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Screen-cell bit layout (16-bit LE, per BG cell):</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Bits</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>0..9</td><td>tile_index (10 bits — into NCGR tilebank)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>10</td><td>hflip</td></tr>
      <tr><td>11</td><td>vflip</td></tr>
      <tr><td>12..15</td><td>palette_bank (4 bits — only used for 4bpp tilesets)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>NANR (RNAN) — animation</h2>
  <p>Type tag <code>rnan</code>. 225 instances.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x00</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>magic = <code>"RNAN"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x10</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>section magic = <code>"KNBA"</code> (ABNK)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x08</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>bank_count</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x0A</code></td><td>2</td><td><code>u16</code></td><td>frame_count_total</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Per-bank entry: frame_count, loop mode, frame data offset. Per-frame entry:
    cell_idx, flag, dx, dy, duration. Animation playback is not yet decoded by
    the project tooling (each cell renders as a static frame).
  </p>

  <h2>Section-magic census</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Section magic</th><th>Resource</th><th>Occurrences</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>RAHC</code></td><td>NCGR CHAR data</td><td>4,338</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>TTLP</code></td><td>NCLR PLTT colors</td><td>2,600</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>PMCP</code></td><td>NCLR palette-bank map</td><td>2,600</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>LBAL</code></td><td>NCER cell labels</td><td>1,778</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>TXEU</code></td><td>NCER user extension</td><td>1,778</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>KBEC</code></td><td>NCER cell block</td><td>1,553</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>NRCS</code></td><td>NSCR screen data</td><td>1,128</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>KNBA</code></td><td>NANR animation bank</td><td>225</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cross-format references</h2>
  <p>
    A composed image requires resolving references across formats:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>NSCR cell.tile_index (10 bits) → tile in NCGR tilebank</li>
    <li>NSCR cell.palette_bank (4 bits) → bank in NCLR (×16 colors)</li>
    <li>NCER OBJ.attr2.tile (10 bits) → tile in NCGR (OBJ mapping aware)</li>
    <li>NCER OBJ.attr2.palette_bank (4 bits) → bank in NCLR</li>
    <li>NCGR ↔ NCLR pairing rules: see <a href={`${base}/field-guide/2d-art/palettes/`}>palette resolution</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>src/translator/_sprite_decode.py</code> — <code>parse_ncgr</code>, <code>parse_nclr</code>, <code>parse_ncer</code>, <code>parse_nscr</code>, <code>compose_*</code></li>
    <li><code>src/translator/_sprite_encode.py</code> — NCGR re-encoder (template-based)</li>
    <li><code>notes/asset_extraction_methodology.md</code> — full pipeline writeup</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
